From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pulsar Bot <pulsar@localhost>
Date: Sat, 08 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] futex: implement futex_waitv syscall (nr 449)

Backport of sys_futex_waitv from Linux 5.16 (kernel/futex/syscalls.c and
waitwake.c) adapted for the 4.19 single-file futex.c.

futex_waitv allows waiting on an array of up to FUTEX_WAITV_MAX (128)
futexes in a single syscall, waking on any of them. Critical for
Wine/Proton/native games via ntsync: games batch waits on many sync
objects, replacing N syscall round-trips with one.

Implementation notes for the 4.19 port:
- Uses existing futex.c helpers (queue_lock/queue_unlock, queue_me,
  unqueue_me, get_futex_value_locked, futex_setup_timer).
- Timeout is absolute; clockid selects CLOCK_MONOTONIC/CLOCK_REALTIME.
- Wire up nr 449 in unistd.h and unistd32.h (arm64 compat).

Signed-off-by: Pulsar Bot <pulsar@localhost>
---
